## What problem(s) does this PR solve?

Optimizes `ContainerTypeValidate` by avoiding unnecessary copies.

Some operations are up to 20% faster from GDScript (up to 30% from C++).

## Additional information

The diff looks scarier than it is. The changes are almost all the same - just using `ContainerTypeValidate` with the new API design.

### Design details

The previous design was to modify a value in-place.
This required making the copy before knowing whether it is even needed.
In addition, converting paths need to sometimes copy the value an additional time.

That design would be appropriate if you already have a buffer and need to modify it in-place. However, in most cases we get a value we cannot modify and need to either reference or copy it. For this, the in-place design is not optimal.

The new design is built around pointers: The untyped / matching paths should short-circuit almost immediately and avoid any copies. 

### Benchmarks

All operations measured are strictly faster than before. The range is from ~1% to ~30% (depending on N, function and caller).
GDScript callers can expect a ~5% "average" improvement when working with arrays and dictionaries.

> **Note:** Benchmarks were written by AI.

